# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore SIDH primefactor, cryptosystems, Buchmann, Dahmen, Nazario, Diffie, DTMs, cryptologists, Homomorphic, Cryptologists, Eliece, Merkle, Isogeny, Supersingular, Zeadally, NTRU, isogeny, Sendrier, Dilithium, SPHINCS, FIPS, Lenstra, Lovász, smallsetminus,Miklós, Ajtai, Lyubashevsky, Micciancio, Díaz, Rolim, Regev, leftarrow, ciphertext, adots, liboqs, Stehle, Schwabe, kems, Decapsulation,recepient, kemalg, decapsulation, Ciphertext, plaintexts, OAEP, trival, ciphertexts, Fujisaki, Okamoto, Eiichiro, Okamato, Tatsuaki, Crytography */}\n"
"In this lesson we will look at how moving to quantum-safe cryptography can protect data today against the threat of quantum algorithms that could break it's protection in future .\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa araling ito, titingnan natin kung paano mapoprotektahan ng paglipat sa "
"quantum-safe na kriptograpiya ang datos ngayon laban sa banta ng mga quantum"
" algorithm na maaaring sirain ang proteksyon nito sa hinaharap.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the end of the lesson we will have covered:\n"
" - What quantum-safe cryptography is\n"
" - Standardization efforts including NIST competitions\n"
" - Mathematical basis of some new algorithms such as Lattices and Learning with Errors\n"
" - Some Python code examples demonstrating how new mathematic challenges can be used for encryption\n"
" - A look at some specific quantum-safe algorithms including those in the CRYSTALS suite\n"
" - Hybrid cryptography\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa katapusan ng aralin, matatalakay na natin ang:\n"
" - Ano ang quantum-safe na kriptograpiya\n"
" - Mga pagsisikap sa pag-standardize kabilang ang mga kompetisyon ng NIST\n"
" - Matematikal na batayan ng ilang bagong algorithm tulad ng Lattices at Learning with Errors\n"
" - Ilang halimbawa ng Python code na nagpapakita kung paano magagamit ang mga bagong matematikal na hamon para sa encryption\n"
" - Isang pagtingin sa ilang partikular na quantum-safe na algorithm kabilang ang mga nasa CRYSTALS suite\n"
" - Hybrid na kriptograpiya\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Introduction to quantum-safe cryptography {#introduction-to-quantum-safe-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Panimula sa quantum-safe na kriptograpiya {#introduction-to-quantum-safe-"
"cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since quantum computers represent a [distinct and potentially more powerful "
"paradigm for "
"computing](https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jap/article/132/16/160902/2837574/The-"
"future-of-quantum-computing-with) than the classical computers in use today,"
" cryptographic security needs to be reassessed for a world where quantum "
"computers may <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The rapid or exponential "
"growth, increase, or multiplication of something, typically in a biological,"
" technological, or abstract context.\">proliferate</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"enabling new cryptographic attacks that would not be possible using "
"classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang mga quantum computer ay kumakatawan sa isang [natatangi at "
"potensyal na mas makapangyarihang paradigma para sa "
"computing](https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jap/article/132/16/160902/2837574/The-"
"future-of-quantum-computing-with) kaysa sa mga klasikal na computer na "
"ginagamit ngayon, kailangang muling tasahin ang kriptograpikong seguridad "
"para sa isang mundo kung saan maaaring <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang "
"mabilis o exponential na paglago, pagtaas, o pagdami ng isang bagay, "
"karaniwang sa biolohikal, teknolohikal, o abstraktong "
"konteksto.\">kumalat</DefinitionTooltip> ang mga quantum computer, na "
"nagbibigay-daan sa mga bagong kriptograpikong atake na hindi posible gamit "
"ang mga klasikal na computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These attacks may occur in future on data that is being transmitted or "
"stored now known as *harvest now, decrypt later*, so it is not sufficient to"
" wait until the required systems are available, but to make changes now.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga atakeng ito ay maaaring mangyari sa hinaharap sa datos na "
"ipinapadala o iniimbak ngayon — kilala bilang *harvest now, decrypt later* —"
" kaya hindi sapat ang maghintay hanggang mayroon nang mga kinakailangang "
"sistema; dapat gumawa ng mga pagbabago ngayon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The field of <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Also known as Post Quantum or "
"Quantum-Resistant. Cryptographic algorithms, protocols, or systems that are "
"designed to withstand attacks from quantum computers. Even as quantum "
"computing technology progresses, the security of digital communication and "
"sensitive information needs to remains intact.\">**quantum-safe "
"cryptography**</DefinitionTooltip> (QSC) encompasses efforts to [identify "
"and develop cryptographic "
"schemes](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7) that can withstand "
"attacks both from quantum and classical computing systems. This is also "
"sometimes called **quantum-resistant**, or **post-quantum cryptography**.`\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang larangan ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Kilala rin bilang Post "
"Quantum o Quantum-Resistant. Mga kriptograpikong algorithm, protokol, o "
"sistema na idinisenyo upang makayanan ang mga atake mula sa mga quantum "
"computer. Kahit na sumulong ang teknolohiya ng quantum computing, ang "
"seguridad ng digital na komunikasyon at sensitibong impormasyon ay "
"nangangailangan na manatiling buo.\">**quantum-safe na "
"kriptograpiya**</DefinitionTooltip> (QSC) ay sumasaklaw sa mga pagsisikap na"
" [tukuyin at bumuo ng mga kriptograpikong "
"pamamaraan](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7) na makakatagal ng mga"
" atake mula sa parehong quantum at klasikal na sistema ng computing. Ito ay "
"tinatawag din minsan na **quantum-resistant**, o **post-quantum "
"cryptography**.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In earlier lessons, we discussed some of the potential security risks that "
"the development of general-purpose quantum computers poses to a number of "
"traditional cryptographic primitives such as symmetric key algorithms, "
"cryptographic hash functions, and asymmetric key algorithms. Additionally, "
"we mentioned cryptographically relevant quantum algorithms and the protocols"
" they impact.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga nakaraang aralin, tinalakay natin ang ilan sa mga potensyal na "
"panganib sa seguridad na dulot ng pagbuo ng mga pangkalahatang quantum "
"computer sa ilang tradisyonal na kriptograpikong primitive tulad ng mga "
"symmetric key algorithm, kriptograpikong hash function, at mga asymmetric "
"key algorithm. Bukod dito, binanggit natin ang mga kriptograpikong may "
"kaugnayan na quantum algorithm at ang mga protokol na kanilang "
"naaapektuhan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that the most significant impacts of quantum algorithms occur in the "
"context of asymmetric key cryptography, where [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) offers a polynomial-"
"time solution to the prime factoring and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Discrete Logarithm Problem. Finding the exponent to which a "
"given number (the base) must be raised to obtain another number (the "
"result), within a specified mathematical group. Solving this problem for "
"certain groups is computationally difficult, forming the basis for several "
"cryptographic schemes but Quantum Computers may have the potential to solve "
"this problem in the future.\">discrete logarithm</DefinitionTooltip> "
"problems. Therefore, asymmetric cryptosystems based on factoring and "
"discrete logarithms need to be replaced by new quantum-safe cryptography "
"schemes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakikita natin na ang pinakamalaking epekto ng mga quantum algorithm ay "
"nagaganap sa konteksto ng asymmetric key cryptography, kung saan ang "
"[algorithm ni Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) ay nag-aalok "
"ng polynomial-time na solusyon sa mga problema ng prime factoring at "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Discrete Logarithm Problem. Ang paghanap ng "
"exponent kung saan dapat itaas ang isang ibinigay na numero (ang base) upang"
" makuha ang isa pang numero (ang resulta), sa loob ng isang tinukoy na "
"matematikal na grupo. Ang paglutas ng problemang ito para sa ilang grupo ay "
"mahirap sa computationally, na bumubuo ng batayan para sa ilang "
"kriptograpikong pamamaraan ngunit ang mga Quantum Computer ay maaaring may "
"kakayahang malutas ang problemang ito sa hinaharap.\">discrete "
"logarithm</DefinitionTooltip>. Samakatuwid, ang mga asymmetric cryptosystem "
"na batay sa factoring at discrete logarithm ay kailangang palitan ng mga "
"bagong quantum-safe na kriptograpikong pamamaraan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is in contrast to the symmetric key and cryptographic hashing protocols"
" impacted by the Grover and [BHT](https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0054319) "
"algorithms, where the quantum speedups are not super-polynomial. Therefore, "
"in this latter case, existing algorithms such as AES and SHA-256 can be "
"fortified at least in the medium term by ensuring sufficiently long key and "
"hash lengths.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay kaibahan sa mga symmetric key at kriptograpikong hashing na protokol "
"na naaapektuhan ng mga algorithm na Grover at "
"[BHT](https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0054319), kung saan ang mga quantum speedup"
" ay hindi super-polynomial. Kaya naman, sa huling kaso, ang mga kasalukuyang"
" algorithm tulad ng AES at SHA-256 ay maaaring palakasin kahit sa "
"katamtamang panahon sa pamamagitan ng pagtiyak ng sapat na haba ng key at "
"hash.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum algorithms and impacts to cryptography {#quantum-algorithms-and-"
"impacts-to-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Mga quantum algorithm at epekto sa kriptograpiya {#quantum-algorithms-and-"
"impacts-to-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Quantum Algorithm | Functionality      | <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"As defined by the [NIST](https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/security_strength): *A number characterizing the amount of work that is expected to suffice to defeat an implemented cryptographic mechanism (for example, by compromising its functionality and/or circumventing the protection that its use was intended to facilitate). Security strength is often expressed in bits. If the security strength of a particular implementation of a cryptographic mechanism is s bits, it is expected that the equivalent of (roughly) 2<sup>s</sup> basic operations of some sort will be sufficient to defeat it in some way.*\">Security Strength</DefinitionTooltip> ($n$ = number of bits) | Impacted Cryptographic Protocols                 | Mitigation             |\n"
"|-------------------|--------------------|------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|------------------------|\n"
"| Shor              | factoring          | $poly(n)$                                            | RSA                                              | Migrate to QSC         |\n"
"| Shor              | discrete logarithm | $poly(n)$                                            | Diffie-Hellman, DSA, Elliptic Curve Cryptography | Migrate to QSC         |\n"
"| Grover            | key search         | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Symmetric key algorithms (for example, AES)             | Sufficient key length  |\n"
"| Grover            | pre-image attack   | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Hash functions (for example, SHA-256)                   | Sufficient hash length |\n"
"| BHT               | collision attack   | $2^{n/3}$ or $2^{2n/5}$                              | Hash functions (for example, SHA-256)                   | Sufficient hash length |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Quantum Algorithm | Functionality      | <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ayon sa kahulugan ng [NIST](https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/security_strength): *Isang numero na nagpapakilala ng dami ng trabaho na inaasahang sapat upang talunin ang isang ipinatupad na kriptograpikong mekanismo (halimbawa, sa pamamagitan ng pagkompromiso ng functionality nito at/o pag-ikot ng proteksyon na nilayong mapadali ng paggamit nito). Ang lakas ng seguridad ay madalas na ipinahayag sa bits. Kung ang lakas ng seguridad ng isang partikular na implementasyon ng isang kriptograpikong mekanismo ay s bits, inaasahan na ang katumbas ng (humigit-kumulang) 2<sup>s</sup> na pangunahing operasyon ng ilang uri ay sapat upang talunin ito sa ilang paraan.*\">Security Strength</DefinitionTooltip> ($n$ = bilang ng bits) | Naaapektuhang Kriptograpikong Protokol                 | Pagpapagaan             |\n"
"|-------------------|--------------------|------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|------------------------|\n"
"| Shor              | factoring          | $poly(n)$                                            | RSA                                              | Lumipat sa QSC         |\n"
"| Shor              | discrete logarithm | $poly(n)$                                            | Diffie-Hellman, DSA, Elliptic Curve Cryptography | Lumipat sa QSC         |\n"
"| Grover            | key search         | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Mga symmetric key algorithm (halimbawa, AES)             | Sapat na haba ng key  |\n"
"| Grover            | pre-image attack   | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Mga hash function (halimbawa, SHA-256)                   | Sapat na haba ng hash |\n"
"| BHT               | collision attack   | $2^{n/3}$ o $2^{2n/5}$                              | Mga hash function (halimbawa, SHA-256)                   | Sapat na haba ng hash |\n"

