# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Computational complexity {#computational-complexity}"
msgstr "Computational complexity {#computational-complexity}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In cryptography, the *computational complexity class* [**NP (non-"
"deterministic polynomial "
"time)**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP_(complexity)&oldid=1158889203)"
" plays an important role. This class consists of decision problems for which"
" proposed solutions can be verified in polynomial time using a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Machine that operates on an infinite tape "
"containing symbols which has a read/write head that can move left or right "
"on the tape and change the symbols according to a set of predetermined "
"rules. In a deterministic Turing machine, the transition from one state to "
"another is uniquely determined by the current state and the symbol being "
"read from the tape. This means that for any given configuration of the "
"machine, there is only one possible next step.\">deterministic Turing "
"machine</DefinitionTooltip> (DTM). The importance of NP stems from the fact "
"that it is conjectured to consist of many computational problems that cannot"
" be solved efficiently by both classical and quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kriptograpiya, ang *computational complexity class* [**NP (non-"
"deterministic polynomial "
"time)**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP_(complexity)&oldid=1158889203)"
" ay may mahalagang papel. Ang klase na ito ay binubuo ng mga desisyon na "
"problema kung saan ang mga iminungkahing solusyon ay maaaring ma-verify sa "
"polynomial na oras gamit ang isang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Makina na"
" gumagana sa isang walang katapusang tape na naglalaman ng mga simbolo na "
"may read/write head na maaaring gumalaw sa kaliwa o kanan sa tape at "
"magpalit ng mga simbolo ayon sa isang hanay ng mga paunang natukoy na "
"panuntunan. Sa isang deterministic na Turing machine, ang paglipat mula sa "
"isang estado patungo sa isa pa ay natatanging tinutukoy ng kasalukuyang "
"estado at ang simbolong binabasa mula sa tape. Nangangahulugan ito na para "
"sa anumang naibigay na konfigurasyong ng makina, mayroon lamang isang "
"posibleng susunod na hakbang.\">deterministic Turing "
"machine</DefinitionTooltip> (DTM). Ang kahalagahan ng NP ay nagmumula sa "
"katotohanan na pinapalagay itong binubuo ng maraming mga computational na "
"problema na hindi maaaring malutas nang mahusay ng parehong klasikal at "
"quantum na computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first generation of successful asymmetric key cryptosystems developed in"
" the 1970s based their security on mathematical problems such as prime "
"factorization and discrete logarithms that are now conjectured to belong to "
"the **NP-intermediate** subclass of NP. This subclass consists of problems "
"that are believed not to have polynomial-time solutions on DTMs but at the "
"same time are also not as hard as the hardest problems in NP.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang henerasyong matagumpay na asymmetric key cryptosystem na binuo "
"noong 1970s ay nagbase ng kanilang seguridad sa mga matematikal na problema "
"tulad ng prime factorization at discrete logarithm na ngayon ay pinapalagay "
"na kabilang sa **NP-intermediate** na subclass ng NP. Ang subclass na ito ay"
" binubuo ng mga problema na pinaniniwalaang walang polynomial-time na "
"solusyon sa mga DTM ngunit sa parehong oras ay hindi rin kasing hirap ng mga"
" pinakamahirap na problema sa NP.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The latter belong to the subclass [**NP-"
"complete**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"completeness&oldid=1157123934). Following [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) in the 1990s, it became"
" clear that at least some NP-intermediate problems are amenable to efficient"
" solutions on quantum computers that are not DTMs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang huli ay kabilang sa subclass na [**NP-"
"complete**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"completeness&oldid=1157123934). Kasunod ng [algorithm ni "
"Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) noong 1990s, naging malinaw "
"na ang ilang NP-intermediate na problema ay madaling malutas sa mga quantum "
"computer na hindi DTM.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, modern quantum-safe cryptography schemes are based on NP-complete"
" problems or related [**NP-"
"hard**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"hardness&oldid=1153995836) problems, which currently are not known to be "
"solvable efficiently even on quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Samakatuwid, ang mga modernong quantum-safe na kriptograpikong pamamaraan ay"
" batay sa mga NP-complete na problema o kaugnay na [**NP-"
"hard**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"hardness&oldid=1153995836) na mga problema, na kasalukuyang hindi kilalang "
"malulutas nang mahusay kahit sa mga quantum computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Average vs worst-case hardness {#average-vs-worst-case-hardness}"
msgstr "Average vs worst-case hardness {#average-vs-worst-case-hardness}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While there are many known NP-hard problems, not every such problem is "
"suitable as a basis for cryptographic security. In this context, the notion "
"of [**average-case "
"hardness**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Computational_hardness_assumption&oldid=1158033193)"
" is useful for cryptography. A problem is **average-case hard** if most "
"instances of the problem drawn randomly from some distribution are hard, "
"whereas a problem is **worst-case hard** if it is hard only on some isolated"
" *worst-case* instances. Quantum-safe cryptologists therefore search for "
"mathematical problems that satisfy the assumption of average-case hardness "
"and employ theoretical tools such as worst-case to average-case "
"[reductions](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) to identify suitable protocols"
" whose security and efficiency can be guaranteed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagama't maraming kilalang NP-hard na problema, hindi bawat problema ay "
"angkop bilang batayan para sa kriptograpikong seguridad. Sa kontekstong ito,"
" ang konsepto ng [**average-case "
"hardness**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Computational_hardness_assumption&oldid=1158033193)"
" ay kapaki-pakinabang para sa kriptograpiya. Ang isang problema ay "
"**average-case hard** kung karamihan sa mga instance ng problema na random "
"na kinukuha mula sa ilang distribusyon ay mahirap, samantalang ang isang "
"problema ay **worst-case hard** kung mahirap lamang ito sa ilang mga "
"nakahiwalay na *worst-case* na instance. Ang mga quantum-safe na "
"kriptolohista kaya ay naghahanap ng mga matematikal na problema na "
"nakakatugon sa pagpapalagay ng average-case hardness at gumagamit ng mga "
"teoretikal na kasangkapan tulad ng worst-case hanggang average-case na [mga "
"reduksyon](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) upang matukoy ang mga angkop na "
"protokol na ang seguridad at kahusayan ay maaaring maging garantisado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical structures {#mathematical-structures}"
msgstr "Mga matematikal na istruktura {#mathematical-structures}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cryptologists have put forth a number of different mathematical structures "
"that satisfy the necessary hardness requirements as potential candidates for"
" quantum-safe migration of asymmetric key cryptosystems. Some well-known "
"families include:\n"
msgstr ""
"Naglagay ang mga kriptolohista ng ilang iba't ibang matematikal na "
"istruktura na nakakatugon sa mga kinakailangang kahirapan bilang mga "
"potensyal na kandidato para sa quantum-safe na paglipat ng mga asymmetric "
"key cryptosystem. Ang ilang kilalang pamilya ay kinabibilangan ng:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Lattice-based cryptography:**](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) This "
"class of algorithms relies on the hardness of problems such as the shortest "
"vector problem (SVP) and the closest vector problem (CVP) in [lattice "
"structures](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)."
" Notable lattice-based schemes include "
"[NTRU](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NTRU&oldid=1107481357) and"
" [Learning with Errors](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26) (LWE).\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Lattice-based na kriptograpiya:**](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) Ang "
"klase ng mga algorithm na ito ay umaasa sa kahirapan ng mga problema tulad "
"ng shortest vector problem (SVP) at closest vector problem (CVP) sa mga "
"[lattice na "
"istruktura](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)."
" Ang mga kapansin-pansing lattice-based na pamamaraan ay kinabibilangan ng "
"[NTRU](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NTRU&oldid=1107481357) at "
"[Learning with Errors](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26) (LWE).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Code-based cryptography:**](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7_4) "
"This type of cryptography is based on the difficulty of decoding a general "
"linear code. The most notable example is the [McEliece "
"cryptosystem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=McEliece_cryptosystem&oldid=1158412532).\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Code-based na "
"kriptograpiya:**](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7_4) Ang uri ng "
"kriptograpiyang ito ay batay sa kahirapan ng pag-decode ng isang "
"pangkalahatang linear code. Ang pinaka-kapansin-pansing halimbawa ay ang "
"[McEliece "
"cryptosystem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=McEliece_cryptosystem&oldid=1158412532).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Multivariate "
"cryptography:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Multivariate_cryptography&oldid=1117344303)"
" These systems involve equations of multiple variables over a finite field. "
"A well-known system in this category is the HFE (Hidden Field Equations) "
"scheme.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Multivariate na "
"kriptograpiya:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Multivariate_cryptography&oldid=1117344303)"
" Ang mga sistemang ito ay nagsasangkot ng mga equation ng maraming variable "
"sa isang finite field. Isang kilalang sistema sa kategoryang ito ay ang HFE "
"(Hidden Field Equations) scheme.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Hash-based "
"cryptography:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hash-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1159153101) These are cryptographic systems that "
"use only cryptographic hash functions. They are often used for digital "
"signatures, like the Merkle signature scheme.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Hash-based na "
"kriptograpiya:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hash-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1159153101) Ito ay mga kriptograpikong sistema na "
"gumagamit lamang ng mga kriptograpikong hash function. Madalas silang "
"ginagamit para sa mga digital na pirma, tulad ng Merkle signature scheme.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Isogeny-based "
"cryptography:**](https://www.computer.org/csdl/magazine/it/2019/06/08896171/1eS9UwZEbjG)"
" These systems are based on the difficulty of certain problems in the "
"algebraic structure of elliptic curves. [Supersingular Isogeny Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Supersingular_isogeny_key_exchange&oldid=1163291033)"
" (SIDH) is an example.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Isogeny-based na "
"kriptograpiya:**](https://www.computer.org/csdl/magazine/it/2019/06/08896171/1eS9UwZEbjG)"
" Ang mga sistemang ito ay batay sa kahirapan ng ilang mga problema sa "
"algebraic na istruktura ng mga elliptic curve. Ang [Supersingular Isogeny "
"Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Supersingular_isogeny_key_exchange&oldid=1163291033)"
" (SIDH) ay isang halimbawa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"NIST standardization of quantum-safe cryptography {#nist-standardization-of-"
"quantum-safe-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Pag-standardize ng NIST sa quantum-safe na kriptograpiya {#nist-"
"standardization-of-quantum-safe-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recognizing the potential impact of quantum computing on current "
"cryptographic systems, NIST initiated a program to standardize quantum-safe "
"cryptographic algorithms in 2016 using a process similar to the one NIST "
"followed to standardize the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) in the early "
"2000s. In an open and transparent process involving security domain "
"stakeholders, several QSC candidates were submitted for evaluation, and "
"following a six-year review process, [NIST announced a list of four "
"finalists](https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2022/07/nist-announces-"
"first-four-quantum-resistant-cryptographic-algorithms) to become a part of "
"NIST’s quantum-safe cryptographic standard.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kinikilala ang potensyal na epekto ng quantum computing sa mga kasalukuyang "
"kriptograpikong sistema, nagsimula ang NIST ng programang mag-standardize ng"
" mga quantum-safe na kriptograpikong algorithm noong 2016 gamit ang "
"prosesong katulad ng sinunod ng NIST upang i-standardize ang Advanced "
"Encryption Standard (AES) noong unang bahagi ng 2000s. Sa isang bukas at "
"transparent na prosesong kinasasangkutan ng mga stakeholder sa larangan ng "
"seguridad, ilang QSC na kandidato ang isinumite para sa pagsusuri, at "
"kasunod ng anim na taong proseso ng pagrerepaso, [inihayag ng NIST ang isang"
" listahan ng apat na finalist](https://www.nist.gov/news-"
"events/news/2022/07/nist-announces-first-four-quantum-resistant-"
"cryptographic-algorithms) na magiging bahagi ng quantum-safe na "
"kriptograpikong pamantayan ng NIST.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finalists of the first NIST quantum-safe cryptography standardization effort"
" {#finalists-of-the-first-nist-quantum-safe-cryptography-standardization-"
"effort}"
msgstr ""
"Mga finalist ng unang pagsisikap ng NIST sa pag-standardize ng quantum-safe "
"na kriptograpiya {#finalists-of-the-first-nist-quantum-safe-cryptography-"
"standardization-effort}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| QSC Algorithm      | Cryptographic family | Application                     |\n"
"|--------------------|----------------------|---------------------------------|\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Kyber     | Lattice-based        | Key encapsulation mechanism     |\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Dilithium | Lattice-based        | Digital signatures              |\n"
"| FALCON             | Lattice-based        | Lightweight digital signatures |\n"
"| SPHINCS+           | Hash-based           | Digital Signatures              |\n"
msgstr ""
"| QSC Algorithm      | Kriptograpikong pamilya | Aplikasyon                     |\n"
"|--------------------|----------------------|---------------------------------|\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Kyber     | Lattice-based        | Key encapsulation mechanism     |\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Dilithium | Lattice-based        | Mga digital na pirma              |\n"
"| FALCON             | Lattice-based        | Magaan na mga digital na pirma |\n"
"| SPHINCS+           | Hash-based           | Mga digital na pirma              |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of the four NIST finalists, three are lattice-based and one, "
"[SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/), is hash-based. The Kyber and Dilithium "
"algorithms, part of the [CRYSTALS cryptographic suite](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/), were selected to be general-purpose protocols for key "
"encapsulation and digital signatures, respectively. "
"[FALCON](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Falcon_(signature_scheme)&oldid=1157852190)"
" was recommended for applications requiring smaller digital signatures than "
"those provided by Dilithium. [SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/) meanwhile was "
"primarily chosen as a backup option to the lattice-based approaches, as it "
"uses a different mathematical structure. Lattice-based cryptography "
"therefore seems well-positioned to form the basis for the first-generation "
"of QSC standards.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa apat na finalist ng NIST, tatlo ang lattice-based at isa, ang "
"[SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/), ay hash-based. Ang mga algorithm na Kyber "
"at Dilithium, bahagi ng [CRYSTALS cryptographic suite](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/), ay pinili bilang mga pangkalahatang protokol para sa key "
"encapsulation at digital na pirma, ayon sa pagkakasunud-sunod. Ang "
"[FALCON](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Falcon_(signature_scheme)&oldid=1157852190)"
" ay inirerekomenda para sa mga aplikasyong nangangailangan ng mas maliliit "
"na digital na pirma kaysa sa ibinibigay ng Dilithium. Ang "
"[SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/) naman ay pangunahing pinili bilang backup "
"na opsyon sa mga lattice-based na pamamaraan, dahil gumagamit ito ng ibang "
"matematikal na istruktura. Ang lattice-based na kriptograpiya ay mukhang "
"handa nang maging batayan para sa unang henerasyong pamantayan ng QSC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In August 2023, [NIST published three draft standards](https://csrc.nist.gov/news/2023/three-draft-fips-for-post-quantum-cryptography) for comments - which include the algorithms above:\n"
"- [FIPS 203, Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 204, Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 205, Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/ipd)\n"
msgstr ""
"Noong Agosto 2023, [nag-publish ang NIST ng tatlong draft na pamantayan](https://csrc.nist.gov/news/2023/three-draft-fips-for-post-quantum-cryptography) para sa mga komento — na kinabibilangan ng mga algorithm sa itaas:\n"
"- [FIPS 203, Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 204, Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 205, Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/ipd)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lattice-based cryptography {#lattice-based-cryptography}"
msgstr "Lattice-based na kriptograpiya {#lattice-based-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the name suggests, [lattice-based "
"cryptography](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1163912863) (LBC) is based on the hardness of "
"certain problems defined on mathematical structures called "
"[**lattices**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985).\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng iminumungkahi ng pangalan, ang [lattice-based na "
"kriptograpiya](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1163912863) (LBC) ay batay sa kahirapan ng ilang "
"partikular na problema na tinukoy sa mga matematikal na istruktura na "
"tinatawag na [**mga "
"lattice**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of fundamental importance are two computational problems on lattices, namely"
" the **shortest vector problem** and the **learning with errors problem**, "
"which we discuss below after some preliminary definitions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ng pangunahing kahalagahan ay dalawang computational na problema sa mga "
"lattice, katulad ng **shortest vector problem** at ang **learning with "
"errors problem**, na tatalakayin natin sa ibaba pagkatapos ng ilang paunang "
"kahulugan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lattices {#lattices}"
msgstr "Mga lattice {#lattices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can think of what a lattice is in the world around us. The Eiffel tower "
"(Paris), or Birds-nest stadium (Beijing). Those structures have many linked "
"elements which can be thought of as a series of points joined together along"
" straight lines.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari tayong mag-isip kung ano ang isang lattice sa mundo sa paligid natin."
" Ang Eiffel tower (Paris), o ang Birds-nest stadium (Beijing). Ang mga "
"istrukturang iyon ay may maraming magkakaugnay na elemento na maaaring "
"isipin bilang isang serye ng mga punto na magkasamang pinagsama sa tuwid na "
"mga linya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diamonds are another form of lattice. There is a clear, repeating structure "
"of Carbon atoms. They are then effectively joined together by atomic bonds; "
"and this structure that is formed is what gives diamond its unique "
"properties. However, different crystal structures can have very different "
"layouts (can be thought of as our lattice structure), and therefore ends up "
"with distinct features. Hence, lattices serve as the foundational "
"mathematical framework that dictates the unique traits of different "
"structures which we use in cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga dyamante ay isa pang anyo ng lattice. Mayroon talagang malinaw, "
"paulit-ulit na istruktura ng mga Carbon atom. Ang mga ito ay epektibong "
"pinagsama ng mga atomic bond; at ang istrukturang nabuo ay siyang nagbibigay"
" sa dyamante ng natatanging katangian nito. Gayunpaman, ang iba't ibang uri "
"ng kristal na istruktura ay maaaring may napaka-kaibang layout (maaaring "
"isipin bilang ating lattice na istruktura), at samakatuwid ay nagtatapos sa "
"mga natatanging katangian. Kaya naman, ang mga lattice ay nagsisilbing "
"pundasyon ng matematikal na balangkas na nagtatakda ng natatanging katangian"
" ng iba't ibang istruktura na ginagamit natin sa kriptograpiya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simple mathematical terms, a lattice can be thought of as a collection of"
" regularly spaced points that repeat at fixed intervals. To describe how "
"these points are positioned relative to each other, we use vectors. The "
"specific arrangement of these vectors, which defines the layout of the "
"lattice, is referred to as the *basis.*\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa simpleng matematikal na termino, ang isang lattice ay maaaring isipin "
"bilang isang koleksyon ng mga regular na nakahanay na punto na paulit-ulit "
"sa mga nakapirming agwat. Upang ilarawan kung paano nakaposisyon ang mga "
"puntong ito kaugnay sa isa't isa, gumagamit tayo ng mga vector. Ang "
"partikular na kaayusan ng mga vector na ito, na nagtatakda ng layout ng "
"lattice, ay tinutukoy bilang *basis*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Imagine you have a box of toy construction bricks, and you want to build "
"various objects with the same set of pieces. Each unique object you create "
"requires a specific arrangement, and the way you choose and arrange the "
"bricks serves as the *basis* for constructing different objects. If you "
"change the selection or arrangement of bricks, you get a different object "
"with distinct characteristics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isipin na mayroon kang kahon ng mga laruan na gawa sa brick, at gusto mong "
"bumuo ng iba't ibang bagay gamit ang parehong hanay ng mga piraso. Ang bawat"
" natatanging bagay na nililikha mo ay nangangailangan ng partikular na "
"kaayusan, at ang paraan ng pagpili at pag-aayos mo ng mga brick ay "
"nagsisilbing *basis* para sa pagtatayo ng iba't ibang bagay. Kung babaguhin "
"mo ang pagpili o kaayusan ng mga brick, makakakuha ka ng ibang bagay na may "
"natatanging katangian.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, in a lattice, the *basis* is like the set of atomic building "
"blocks that define the lattice's structure. Depending on how you arrange "
"these building blocks (atoms or points) in the lattice, you can create "
"various lattice structures with different properties. Just as changing the "
"toy construction brick pieces changes the object you build, altering the "
"basis changes the lattice's characteristics and properties.\n"
msgstr ""
"Katulad nito, sa isang lattice, ang *basis* ay parang hanay ng mga atomic "
"building block na nagtatakda ng istruktura ng lattice. Depende sa kung paano"
" mo ina-ayos ang mga building block na ito (mga atom o punto) sa lattice, "
"maaari kang lumikha ng iba't ibang lattice na istruktura na may iba't ibang "
"katangian. Tulad ng pagbabago ng mga piraso ng brick na laruan na nagpapalit"
" ng bagay na nito, ang pagbabago ng basis ay nagbabago ng mga katangian at "
"ari-arian ng lattice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's important to note that lattices are not limited to two or three "
"dimensions; they can extend to higher dimensions, and in fields like "
"cryptography, they may involve 1000s or more dimensions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mahalagang tandaan na ang mga lattice ay hindi limitado sa dalawa o tatlong "
"dimensyon; maaari silang mag-extend sa mas mataas na dimensyon, at sa mga "
"larangan tulad ng kriptograpiya, maaari silang sumasaklaw ng 1000s o higit "
"pang dimensyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of lattices\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na paglalarawan ng mga lattice\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given $n$ linearly independent vectors $A = "
"\\{\\mathbf{v_1},...,\\mathbf{v_n} | \\mathbf{v_i} \\in \\mathbb{R}^m\\}$, "
"the *lattice* $\\mathcal{L}$ generated by $A$ is the set of integer linear "
"combinations $\\mathcal{L} = \\{ \\sum_i c_i \\mathbf{v_i} | c_i \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z} \\}$\n"
msgstr ""
"Binigyan ng $n$ linearly independent na vector $A = "
"\\{\\mathbf{v_1},...,\\mathbf{v_n} | \\mathbf{v_i} \\in \\mathbb{R}^m\\}$, "
"ang *lattice* $\\mathcal{L}$ na nabuo ng $A$ ay ang hanay ng integer linear "
"combination $\\mathcal{L} = \\{ \\sum_i c_i \\mathbf{v_i} | c_i \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z} \\}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A *basis* $B$ of a lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ is any set of linearly independent"
" vectors $B=\\{b_1,...,b_n\\}$  that spans the lattice i.e, $\\mathcal{L}(B)"
" = \\{ \\sum_i z_i b_i | z_i \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang *basis* $B$ ng isang lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ ay anumang hanay ng "
"linearly independent na vector $B=\\{b_1,...,b_n\\}$ na sumasaklaw sa "
"lattice, ibig sabihin, $\\mathcal{L}(B) = \\{ \\sum_i z_i b_i | z_i \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z} \\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Importantly, the basis for a given lattice is not unique. Two different "
"basis sets $B, B^{\\prime}$ can describe the same lattice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mahalagang tandaan, ang basis para sa isang ibinigay na lattice ay hindi "
"natatangi. Dalawang magkaibang hanay ng basis $B, B^{\\prime}$ ay maaaring "
"maglalarawan ng parehong lattice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not every basis is unique - it may just be a different perspective of the "
"same structure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi bawat basis ay natatangi — maaaring iba lang itong pananaw ng parehong"
" istruktura.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This leads to an important concept in lattice mathematics, that of "
"[*lattice-basis "
"reduction*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_reduction&oldid=1139588628)."
" This is the process of taking a given integer lattice and attempting to "
"find a *good* basis comprising short, nearly orthogonal vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay humahantong sa isang mahalagang konsepto sa matematika ng lattice, "
"ang tinatawag na [*lattice-basis "
"reduction*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_reduction&oldid=1139588628)."
" Ito ang proseso ng pagkuha ng isang ibinigay na integer lattice at "
"pagtatangkang mahanap ang isang *magandang* basis na binubuo ng mga maikli, "
"halos orthogonal na vector.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 1: Lattice-basis reduction in two dimensions from a \"bad\" basis v_1,"
" v_2 to a good basis u_1, u_2](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/Lattice-reduction-wiki.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 1: Lattice-basis reduction sa dalawang dimensyon mula sa isang "
"\"masamang\" basis v_1, v_2 patungo sa isang magandang basis u_1, "
"u_2](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/Lattice-reduction-wiki.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 1. Lattice-basis reduction in two dimensions from a \"bad\" basis "
"$v_1$, $v_2$ to a good basis $u_1$, $u_2$*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Figure 1. Lattice-basis reduction sa dalawang dimensyon mula sa isang "
"\"masamang\" basis $v_1$, $v_2$ patungo sa isang magandang basis $u_1$, "
"$u_2$*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lattice-basis reductions can be performed in polynomial-time using the "
"[**Lenstra–Lenstra–Lovász** "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lenstra%E2%80%93Lenstra%E2%80%93Lov%C3%A1sz_lattice_basis_reduction_algorithm&oldid=1151925724)"
" (LLL).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga lattice-basis reduction ay maaaring isagawa sa polynomial na oras "
"gamit ang [**Lenstra–Lenstra–Lovász** "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lenstra%E2%80%93Lenstra%E2%80%93Lov%C3%A1sz_lattice_basis_reduction_algorithm&oldid=1151925724)"
" (LLL).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The shortest vector problem {#the-shortest-vector-problem}"
msgstr "Ang shortest vector problem {#the-shortest-vector-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **shortest vector problem** (SVP) is the challenge of finding the "
"shortest distance (vector), between any two points in the lattice\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **shortest vector problem** (SVP) ay ang hamon ng paghanap ng "
"pinakamaikling distansya (vector) sa pagitan ng anumang dalawang punto sa "
"lattice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of the SVP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na paglalarawan ng SVP\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given a lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ embedded in a vector space $\\mathcal{V}$ "
"with norm $N$, the "
"[SVP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)"
" asks for the shortest non-zero vector in $\\mathcal{L}$ as measured by $N$,"
" that is, find a vector $v$ such that its length $\\|v\\|_N = "
"\\min\\limits_{v^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L} \\smallsetminus "
"\\{\\mathbf{0}\\}} \\|v^{\\prime}\\|_N = \\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binigyan ng isang lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ na nakabaon sa isang vector space "
"$\\mathcal{V}$ na may norm $N$, ang "
"[SVP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)"
" ay humihingi ng pinakamaikiling hindi-zero na vector sa $\\mathcal{L}$ na "
"sinusukat ng $N$, iyon ay, hanapin ang isang vector $v$ na ang haba nito "
"$\\|v\\|_N = \\min\\limits_{v^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L} \\smallsetminus "
"\\{\\mathbf{0}\\}} \\|v^{\\prime}\\|_N = \\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 2: The SVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors b_1, b_2: The "
"orange vector is the shortest vector](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/SVP.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 2: Ang SVP sa isang lattice na tinukoy ng mga basis vector na b_1, "
"b_2: Ang orange na vector ay ang pinakamaikling "
"vector](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/SVP.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 2. The SVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors $b_1$, $b_2$: The"
" yellow vector is the shortest vector*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Figure 2. Ang SVP sa isang lattice na tinukoy ng mga basis vector na $b_1$,"
" $b_2$: Ang dilaw na vector ay ang pinakamaikling vector*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Miklós Ajtai has shown that the shortest vector problem is **NP-"
"hard**](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/237814.237838) in the worst case for "
"certain random lattices, even when lattice-basis reduction to a *good* basis"
" is possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Ipinakita ni Miklós Ajtai na ang shortest vector problem ay **NP-"
"hard**](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/237814.237838) sa worst case para sa "
"ilang random na lattice, kahit na posible ang lattice-basis reduction "
"patungo sa isang *magandang* basis.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ajtai also demonstrated that there exists a worst-case to average-case "
"reduction for the shortest vector problem, laying the foundation for its use"
" in cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinakita rin ni Ajtai na may worst-case hanggang average-case na reduksyon "
"para sa shortest vector problem, na nagtatag ng pundasyon para sa paggamit "
"nito sa kriptograpiya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The closest vector problem {#the-closest-vector-problem}"
msgstr "Ang closest vector problem {#the-closest-vector-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the **closest vector problem** (CVP) we are looking to find the closest "
"point on the lattice to the origin, or location given.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa **closest vector problem** (CVP), naghahanap tayo ng pinakamalapit na "
"punto sa lattice patungo sa pinagmulan, o ibinigay na lokasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The CVP is also known to be NP-hard.\n"
msgstr "Ang CVP ay kilala rin na NP-hard.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 3: The CVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors b_1, b_2: The red "
"point represents the closest lattice vector to the given external vector "
"shown in green that is not on the lattice](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/CVP.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 3: Ang CVP sa isang lattice na tinukoy ng mga basis vector na b_1, "
"b_2: Ang pulang punto ay kumakatawan sa pinakamalapit na lattice vector sa "
"ibinigay na panlabas na vector na ipinapakita sa berde na hindi nasa "
"lattice](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/CVP.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 3. The CVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors $b_1$, $b_2$: The"
" red point represents the closest lattice vector to the given external "
"vector shown in green that is not on the lattice*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Figure 3. Ang CVP sa isang lattice na tinukoy ng mga basis vector na $b_1$,"
" $b_2$: Ang pulang punto ay kumakatawan sa pinakamalapit na lattice vector "
"sa ibinigay na panlabas na vector na ipinapakita sa berde na hindi nasa "
"lattice*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *shortest vector problem* is a special case of the *closest vector "
"problem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang *shortest vector problem* ay isang espesyal na kaso ng *closest vector "
"problem*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of CVP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na paglalarawan ng CVP\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ embedded in a vector space $\\mathcal{V}$ with "
"metric $M$ is given, along with a vector $v$ in $\\mathcal{V}$ but not "
"necessarily in $\\mathcal{L}$. The task then is to find the vector $u$ in "
"$\\mathcal{L}$ closest to $v$ as measured by $M$ that is, $d_M (u, v) = "
"\\min\\limits_{u^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L}} d_M(u^{\\prime}, v)$ where "
"$d_M$ is the distance function of the metric $M$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibinibigay ang isang lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ na nakabaon sa isang vector "
"space $\\mathcal{V}$ na may metric $M$, kasama ang isang vector $v$ sa "
"$\\mathcal{V}$ ngunit hindi kinakailangang nasa $\\mathcal{L}$. Ang gawain "
"ay hanapin ang vector $u$ sa $\\mathcal{L}$ na pinakamalapit sa $v$ na "
"sinusukat ng $M$, iyon ay, $d_M (u, v) = \\min\\limits_{u^{\\prime} \\in "
"\\mathcal{L}} d_M(u^{\\prime}, v)$ kung saan ang $d_M$ ay ang distance "
"function ng metric $M$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bounded distance decoding problem {#the-bounded-distance-decoding-"
"problem}"
msgstr ""
"Ang bounded distance decoding problem {#the-bounded-distance-decoding-"
"problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Very similar to the CVP is the [**bounded distance "
"decoding**](https://doi.org/10.1007/11830924_41) (BDD) problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Katulad ng CVP ay ang [**bounded distance "
"decoding**](https://doi.org/10.1007/11830924_41) (BDD) problem.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case we know that the origin supplied is close to the lattice, but "
"not *how close*, ie *bounded*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kasong ito, alam natin na ang ibinigay na pinagmulan ay malapit sa "
"lattice, ngunit hindi *gaano kalayo*, ibig sabihin, *bounded*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of the BDD problem\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na paglalarawan ng BDD problem\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is additionally specified that the external vector $v$ is at most within "
"a distance $\\sigma\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$, where $\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$ "
"is the length of the shortest vector in the lattice and $\\sigma$ is a small"
" parameter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod pa rito, tinukoy na ang panlabas na vector $v$ ay nasa loob ng "
"pinakamataas na distansyang $\\sigma\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$, kung saan ang "
"$\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$ ay ang haba ng pinakamaikling vector sa lattice at "
"ang $\\sigma$ ay isang maliit na parameter.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The learning with errors problem {#the-learning-with-errors-problem}"
msgstr "Ang learning with errors problem {#the-learning-with-errors-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The learning with errors (LWE) problem is based on the mathematics of "
"lattices combined with the idea of introducing errors into an equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang learning with errors (LWE) problem ay batay sa matematika ng mga lattice"
" na pinagsama sa ideya ng pagpapakilala ng mga error sa isang equation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As is the case with any mathematical basis for cryptographic algorithms we "
"can easily introduce noise as we make a series of calculations, but trying "
"to find the inverse is very difficult.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng kaso sa anumang matematikal na batayan para sa mga kriptograpikong "
"algorithm, madali tayong makapagpapakilala ng ingay habang gumagawa ng isang"
" serye ng mga kalkulasyon, ngunit ang pagsubok na hanapin ang inverse ay "
"napakahirap.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics of the LWE problem\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematika ng LWE problem\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [learning with errors "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Learning_with_errors&amp;oldid=1153719613)"
" ${\\mathrm{LWE}_{q,\\chi}}$ with modulus $q$ and error distribution $\\chi$"
" is: Given access only to polynomially many samples $(\\mathbf {a} ,t)$ of "
"choice from Alice's distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$, \"learn\" and "
"output the secret vector ${\\mathbf{s}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [learning with errors "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Learning_with_errors&amp;oldid=1153719613)"
" ${\\mathrm{LWE}_{q,\\chi}}$ na may modulus $q$ at error distribution "
"$\\chi$ ay: Binibigyan ng access lamang sa polynomial na maraming sample "
"$(\\mathbf {a} ,t)$ na pinili mula sa distribusyon ni Alice "
"$A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$, \"matutunan\" at i-output ang secret vector "
"${\\mathbf{s}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let ${\\mathbb {Z} _{q}}$ be the ring of integers modulo $q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hayaan ang ${\\mathbb {Z} _{q}}$ na maging ring ng mga integer modulo $q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let ${\\mathbb {Z}_{q}^{n}}$ be the set of $n$-dimensional vectors over "
"${\\displaystyle \\mathbb{Z}_{q}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hayaan ang ${\\mathbb {Z}_{q}^{n}}$ na maging hanay ng $n$-dimensional na "
"vector sa ${\\displaystyle \\mathbb{Z}_{q}}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An adversary — say, Alice — chooses a fixed vector ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$ and keeps it a secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang kalaban — sabihin nating si Alice — ay pumipili ng isang "
"nakapirming vector ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in {\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$ at "
"iniingatan itong lihim.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice also specifies $\\chi$, a fixed \"error\" probability distribution "
"over $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinukoy din ni Alice ang $\\chi$, isang nakapirming \"error\" na probability"
" distribution sa $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the above ingredients, she constructs a distribution "
"$A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ on ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}\\times{\\mathbb {Z} "
"_{q}}$ as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamit ang mga sangkap sa itaas, nagtatayo siya ng distribusyon "
"$A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ sa ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}\\times{\\mathbb {Z} "
"_{q}}$ tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the uniform distribution over ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$, Alice chooses a "
"vector ${\\mathbf{a}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ .\n"
msgstr ""
"Mula sa uniform distribution sa ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$, pumipili si Alice "
"ng isang vector ${\\mathbf{a}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the given distribution $\\chi$, she picks a number $ {\\displaystyle "
"\\varepsilon \\in \\mathbb {Z} _{q} }$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mula sa ibinigay na distribusyon $\\chi$, pumipili siya ng numero $ "
"{\\displaystyle \\varepsilon \\in \\mathbb {Z} _{q} }$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"She then evaluates ${\\displaystyle t=\\langle \\mathbf{a} ,\\mathbf {s} "
"\\rangle + \\varepsilon}$, where $\\langle\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{s}\\rangle "
"=\\sum_i a_{i}s_{i}$ is the standard inner product on "
"${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ and the addition is in $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos ay sinusuri niya ang ${\\displaystyle t=\\langle \\mathbf{a} "
",\\mathbf {s} \\rangle + \\varepsilon}$, kung saan ang "
"$\\langle\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{s}\\rangle =\\sum_i a_{i}s_{i}$ ay ang "
"karaniwang inner product sa ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ at ang karagdagan ay "
"nasa $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice outputs ${\\displaystyle (\\mathbf {a} ,t)}$.\n"
msgstr "Ini-output ni Alice ang ${\\displaystyle (\\mathbf {a} ,t)}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    Note the errors introduced: $\\varepsilon$ drawn from $\\chi$\n"
msgstr ""
"    Tandaan ang mga error na ipinakilala: $\\varepsilon$ na kinuha mula sa "
"$\\chi$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Early developments in the LWE problem employed the one-dimensional "
"discrete Gaussian distribution on $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$ as the error "
"distribution.\n"
msgstr ""
"    Ang mga maagang pag-unlad sa LWE problem ay gumamit ng one-dimensional "
"discrete Gaussian distribution sa $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$ bilang error "
"distribution.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The remarkable feature of the LWE problem is that without the errors, it "
"reduces to a set of linear equations that can be easily solved using a "
"technique like Gaussian elimination.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang kapansin-pansing katangian ng LWE problem ay na nang wala ang mga error,"
" ito ay nagreresulta sa isang hanay ng mga linear na equation na madaling "
"malutas gamit ang isang technique tulad ng Gaussian elimination.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, the inclusion of a suitable error distribution renders it an NP-"
"hard problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayunpaman, ang pagsasama ng isang angkop na error distribution ay ginagawa "
"itong isang NP-hard na problema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encryption using the Learning with Errors cryptosystem {#encryption-using-"
"the-learning-with-errors-cryptosystem}"
msgstr ""
"Encryption gamit ang Learning with Errors cryptosystem {#encryption-using-"
"the-learning-with-errors-cryptosystem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LWE problem discussed above leads to a public key cryptosystem "
"introduced by [Regev](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang LWE problem na tinalakay sa itaas ay humahantong sa isang public key "
"cryptosystem na ipinakilala ni "
"[Regev](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The exact process will be covered in the Python example below.\n"
msgstr "Ang eksaktong proseso ay tatalakayin sa halimbawa ng Python sa ibaba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics of key generation, encryption, and decryption\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematika ng key generation, encryption, at decryption\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Parameters:** The cryptosystem is characterized by the vector dimension or"
" security parameter $n$, modulus $q$, number of LWE samples $N$, and error "
"distribution $\\chi$. Typical choices that guarantee both security and "
"correctness are:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga parameter:** Ang cryptosystem ay nailalarawan ng vector dimension o "
"security parameter $n$, modulus $q$, bilang ng LWE sample $N$, at error "
"distribution $\\chi$. Ang mga tipikal na pagpipilian na nagga-garantiya ng "
"parehong seguridad at kawastuhan ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$q$ is a prime between $n^2$ and $2n^2$\n"
msgstr "$q$ ay isang prime sa pagitan ng $n^2$ at $2n^2$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$N = 1.1\\cdot~n~log~q$\n"
msgstr "$N = 1.1\\cdot~n~log~q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\chi = \\Psi_{\\alpha}$, with $\\alpha = 1/(\\sqrt{n}~log^2{n})$, where "
"$\\Psi_{\\alpha}$ is obtained by sampling the normal distribution "
"$\\mathcal{N}(0, \\alpha^2/(2\\pi))$ and reducing the result modulo 1\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\chi = \\Psi_{\\alpha}$, na may $\\alpha = 1/(\\sqrt{n}~log^2{n})$, kung "
"saan ang $\\Psi_{\\alpha}$ ay nakuha sa pamamagitan ng pag-sample sa normal "
"distribution $\\mathcal{N}(0, \\alpha^2/(2\\pi))$ at pagbabago ng resulta "
"modulo 1\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Private key:** The private key is the secret vector ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Private key:** Ang private key ay ang secret vector ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Public key:** Choose $N$ samples $(\\mathbf{a}_i ,b_i)_{i=1}^N$ from the "
"LWE distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Public key:** Pumili ng $N$ na sample $(\\mathbf{a}_i ,b_i)_{i=1}^N$ mula "
"sa LWE distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Encryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Encryption:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encryption utilizes the public key and is carried out bit by bit.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang encryption ng public key at isinasagawa ito bit-by-bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each bit of the message, randomly choose a binary vector $\\mathbf{r} "
"\\in \\{0,1\\}^N$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa bawat bit ng mensahe, random na pumili ng binary vector $\\mathbf{r}"
" \\in \\{0,1\\}^N$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the message bit is 0, the encryption is $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang message bit ay 0, ang encryption ay $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the message bit is 1, the encryption is $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\lfloor \\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor + \\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang message bit ay 1, ang encryption ay $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\lfloor \\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor + \\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Decryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Decryption:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The decryption utilizes the private key ${\\mathbf{s}}$.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang decryption ng private key ${\\mathbf{s}}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pair $({\\mathbf{a}, b })$ decrypts to $0$ if $b-\\langle "
"\\mathbf{a}\\cdot\\mathbf{s}\\rangle$ is closer to $0$ than "
"$\\lfloor\\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor$ modulo $q$, else it decrypts to 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pares $({\\mathbf{a}, b })$ ay nag-decrypt sa $0$ kung ang $b-\\langle "
"\\mathbf{a}\\cdot\\mathbf{s}\\rangle$ ay mas malapit sa $0$ kaysa "
"$\\lfloor\\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor$ modulo $q$, kung hindi, nag-decrypt ito sa "
"1.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The security of the LWE public key cryptosystem was analyzed by Regev:\n"
msgstr "Ang seguridad ng LWE public key cryptosystem ay sinuri ni Regev:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Firstly, it was shown that recovering the error/noise vector $\\mathbf{e} = "
"[\\varepsilon_1,...,\\varepsilon_N] \\leftarrow \\chi^N$ involved in the "
"construction of the public key is as hard as the bounded distance decoding "
"(BDD) problem, which, as noted above, is believed to be NP-hard. This "
"establishes the correspondence between LWE and explicit lattice problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, ipinakita na ang pagbawi ng error/noise vector $\\mathbf{e} = "
"[\\varepsilon_1,...,\\varepsilon_N] \\leftarrow \\chi^N$ na kasangkot sa "
"pagtatayo ng public key ay kasing hirap ng bounded distance decoding (BDD) "
"problem, na, gaya ng nabanggit sa itaas, ay pinaniniwalaang NP-hard. "
"Itinatag nito ang ugnayan sa pagitan ng LWE at mga eksplisit na lattice na "
"problema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Secondly, security against chosen plain text attacks (CPA) is based on the "
"observation that an algorithm for distinguishing between encryptions of 0 "
"and 1 in the above cryptosystem can also distinguish between the "
"distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ and the uniform distribution over "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{q}$, which would imply a solution "
"of LWE itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pangalawa, ang seguridad laban sa mga chosen plain text attack (CPA) ay "
"batay sa pagmamasid na ang isang algorithm para sa pagkakakilala sa pagitan "
"ng mga encryption ng 0 at 1 sa cryptosystem sa itaas ay maaari ring makilala"
" sa pagitan ng distribusyon $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ at ng uniform "
"distribution sa $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{q}$, na "
"magsasangkot ng solusyon sa LWE mismo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Illustration of LWE encryption in Python {#illustration-of-lwe-encryption-"
"in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Paglalarawan ng LWE encryption sa Python {#illustration-of-lwe-encryption-"
"in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following simple example shows the use of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Learning With Errors. A mathematical technique which hides "
"secret information by introducing errors into equations, making them harder "
"to solve.\">LWE</DefinitionTooltip> for encryption and decryption. Bob will "
"send an encrypted message to Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na simpleng halimbawa ay nagpapakita ng paggamit ng "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Learning With Errors. Isang matematikal na "
"technique na nagtatago ng lihim na impormasyon sa pamamagitan ng "
"pagpapakilala ng mga error sa mga equation, na ginagawa itong mas mahirap "
"malutas.\">LWE</DefinitionTooltip> para sa encryption at decryption. "
"Magpapadala si Bob ng naka-encrypt na mensahe kay Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice and Bob agree on the **problem parameters**. These are "
"explained in detail in the maths section above, but in summary we require "
"$n, q, N, \\chi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, magkakasundo sina Alice at Bob sa **mga parameter ng problema**. Ang "
"mga ito ay detalyadong ipinaliwanag sa seksyon ng matematika sa itaas, "
"ngunit sa buod kailangan natin ng $n, q, N, \\chi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We start with some of the basic parameters\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayo sa ilan sa mga pangunahing parameter:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$N$ represents the number of samples\n"
msgstr "Ang $N$ ay kumakatawan sa bilang ng mga sample\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$q$ is a modulus\n"
msgstr "Ang $q$ ay isang modulus\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "n is known as the security parameter, or vector dimension.\n"
msgstr "Ang n ay kilala bilang ang security parameter, o vector dimension.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "These parameters are all public information in principle.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga parameter na ito ay lahat pampublikong impormasyon sa prinsipyo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We also need a way of introducing errors\n"
msgstr "Kailangan din natin ng paraan ng pagpapakilala ng mga error.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $\\chi$ represent the errors we want to introduce - we use a discrete "
"Gaussian distribution on $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}$ characterized by mean 0 and "
"standard deviation $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito ang $\\chi$ ay kumakatawan sa mga error na gusto nating ipakilala — "
"gumagamit tayo ng discrete Gaussian distribution sa $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}$ na "
"nailalarawan ng mean na 0 at standard deviation na $\\sigma$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This definition of the errors to introduce is also public.\n"
msgstr "Ang kahulugan ng mga error na ipapakilala ay pampubliko rin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So in Python, we need a simple function that approximates random error/noise"
" contributions $\\varepsilon$ drawn from a discrete Gaussian distribution "
"$\\chi$ with standard deviation $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya sa Python, kailangan natin ng simpleng function na humahampas ng random"
" na error/noise contribution $\\varepsilon$ mula sa isang discrete Gaussian "
"distribution $\\chi$ na may standard deviation na $\\sigma$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some example values are printed so that you can see the distribution around "
"0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ilang halimbawa ng mga value ay naka-print para makita mo ang "
"distribusyon sa paligid ng 0.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next, Alice needs to generate her key pair.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, kailangang bumuo ni Alice ng key pair niya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"She sets up her **private key** by choosing $n$ values between 0 and $q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Itinatakda niya ang kanyang **private key** sa pamamagitan ng pagpili ng $n$"
" na value sa pagitan ng 0 at $q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice now sets up her **public key**, by choosing random vectors, which are "
"then combined with the generated errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay itinatakda ni Alice ang kanyang **public key**, sa pamamagitan ng "
"pagpili ng mga random na vector, na pagkatapos ay pinagsama sa mga nabuong "
"error.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematika\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "More precisely, she needs to generate the sample $A_{s,\\chi}$.\n"
msgstr "Mas tiyak, kailangan niyang buuin ang sample $A_{s,\\chi}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Accordingly, she randomly chooses vectors $\\mathbf{a} \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n}$ and errors $\\varepsilon$ from $\\chi$ to construct $N$"
" samples $(\\mathbf{a}, b)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alinsunod dito, random niyang pinipili ang mga vector $\\mathbf{a} \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n}$ at mga error $\\varepsilon$ mula sa $\\chi$ upang "
"makabuo ng $N$ na sample $(\\mathbf{a}, b)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice can now share her public key.\n"
msgstr "Maaari na ngayong ibahagi ni Alice ang kanyang public key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob can now use this to send Alice an encrypted message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na ngayong gamitin ito ni Bob upang magpadala ng naka-encrypt na "
"mensahe kay Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob's message is a single bit.\n"
msgstr "Ang mensahe ni Bob ay isang solong bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To encrypt the message, Bob needs to select an arbitrary number of samples "
"at random from Alice's public key to form the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang i-encrypt ang mensahe, kailangang pumili si Bob ng arbitrary na bilang"
" ng mga sample nang random mula sa public key ni Alice upang mabuo ang "
"ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For this, he creates a mask, a random binary vector $r$ of length $N$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para dito, lumilikha siya ng mask, isang random na binary vector $r$ na may "
"haba na $N$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now take this mask and apply it to the relevant entry in Alice's public "
"key, calculating a sum of the values found.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay kinukuha natin ang mask na ito at inilalapat ito sa kaugnay na "
"entry sa public key ni Alice, at kinakalkula ang kabuuan ng mga value na "
"natagpuan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob broadcasts the ciphertext, which Alice can decrypt using her "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, ibi-broadcast ni Bob ang ciphertext, na maaaring i-decrypt ni "
"Alice gamit ang kanyang private key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since this protocol works bit by bit for encrypting longer bit strings, we "
"simply repeat the operations in a loop. The following shows a scenario where"
" Bob wishes to transfer 16 encrypted bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang protokol na ito ay gumagana bit-by-bit para sa pag-encrypt ng mas "
"mahabang bit string, simpleng inuulit natin ang mga operasyon sa isang loop."
" Ang sumusunod ay nagpapakita ng isang sitwasyon kung saan nais ni Bob na "
"maglipat ng 16 naka-encrypt na bit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Module-LWE and the CRYSTALS suite {#module-lwe-and-the-crystals-suite}"
msgstr "Module-LWE at ang CRYSTALS suite {#module-lwe-and-the-crystals-suite}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The learning with errors (LWE) problem, introduced in a simplified form "
"above and generally valid on arbitrary lattices, has been extended to "
"algebraic *rings* within the so-called [**Ring-"
"LWE**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ring_learning_with_errors&oldid=1148731729)"
" framework primarily to improve the efficiency of resulting cryptosystems. "
"However, the extra algebraic structure of Ring-LWE may be potentially "
"exploitable, even though no such exploits are currently known.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang learning with errors (LWE) problem, na ipinakita sa simplified na anyo "
"sa itaas at karaniwang valid sa mga arbitrary na lattice, ay pinalawak na "
"para sa mga algebraic na *ring* sa loob ng tinatawag na [**Ring-"
"LWE**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ring_learning_with_errors&oldid=1148731729)"
" framework — pangunahin para mapabuti ang kahusayan ng mga cryptosystem na "
"resulta nito. Gayunpaman, ang karagdagang algebraic na istraktura ng Ring-"
"LWE ay posibleng mapagsasamantalahan, kahit wala pang natuklasang ganitong "
"pagsasamantala sa kasalukuyan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two of the four finalists in NIST's QSC standardization process — namely, "
"the [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) key "
"encapsulation mechanism (KEM) and the [**CRYSTALS-Dilithium**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/dilithium/index.shtml) digital signature protocol — are based "
"on structures known as <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Collection of all "
"submodules of a given module. A submodule is a subset of the module that "
"itself forms a module under the same operations. The set of all submodules "
"forms a lattice, which is a partially ordered set where any two elements "
"have a unique least upper bound and greatest lower bound.\">*module "
"lattices*</DefinitionTooltip> and the related [**Module-"
"LWE**](https://eprint.iacr.org/2012/090).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalawa sa apat na finalista sa proseso ng NIST QSC standardization — ang "
"[**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) key "
"encapsulation mechanism (KEM) at ang [**CRYSTALS-Dilithium**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/dilithium/index.shtml) digital signature protocol — ay "
"nakabatay sa mga istrakturang kilala bilang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Collection of all submodules of a given module. A submodule is "
"a subset of the module that itself forms a module under the same operations."
" The set of all submodules forms a lattice, which is a partially ordered set"
" where any two elements have a unique least upper bound and greatest lower "
"bound.\">*module lattices*</DefinitionTooltip> at sa kaugnay na [**Module-"
"LWE**](https://eprint.iacr.org/2012/090).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We refer interested readers to specialized courses on these topics for the "
"mathematical details but note here that Module-LWE is seen as a compromise "
"between LWE and Ring-LWE. It provides more efficiency than LWE (though less "
"than Ring-LWE) but also gives a higher level of security assurance than "
"Ring-LWE because it does not rely as heavily on the algebraic structure of "
"the problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa mga interesadong mambabasa, inirekomenda namin ang mga "
"espesyalisadong kurso sa mga paksang ito para sa mga detalyeng matematikal, "
"ngunit dapat tandaan dito na ang Module-LWE ay itinuturing na kompromiso sa "
"pagitan ng LWE at Ring-LWE. Nagbibigay ito ng mas mataas na kahusayan kaysa "
"sa LWE (kahit mas mababa kaysa sa Ring-LWE) ngunit nagbibigay din ng mas "
"mataas na antas ng tiwala sa seguridad kaysa sa Ring-LWE dahil hindi ito "
"masyadong umaasa sa algebraic na istraktura ng problema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Key Encapsulation Mechanisms and CRYSTALS-Kyber {#key-encapsulation-"
"mechanisms-and-crystals-kyber}"
msgstr ""
"Mga Key Encapsulation Mechanism at CRYSTALS-Kyber {#key-encapsulation-"
"mechanisms-and-crystals-kyber}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Traditional asymmetric key cryptosystems are most heavily deployed for their"
" *key-exchange* and *digital signature* functionalities and as such, the "
"NIST standardization process sought to develop quantum-safe alternatives for"
" these two functionalities. The [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) protocol is therefore designed as a "
"dedicated [**Key Encapsulation "
"Mechanism**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965)"
" (KEM) rather than as a general purpose encryption scheme such as RSA. A "
"workflow illustrating the use of Kyber to establish a shared secret between "
"two parties is shown below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga tradisyonal na asymmetric key cryptosystem ay karaniwang ginagamit "
"para sa kanilang mga functionality na *key-exchange* at *digital signature*,"
" kaya naman hinahangad ng proseso ng NIST standardization na makabuo ng mga "
"quantum-safe na alternatibo para sa dalawang functionality na ito. Ang "
"[**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) protocol ay "
"dinisenyo bilang isang dedicated [**Key Encapsulation "
"Mechanism**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965)"
" (KEM) at hindi bilang isang pangkalahatang encryption scheme tulad ng RSA. "
"Ang isang workflow na nagpapakita ng paggamit ng Kyber para maitatag ang "
"shared secret sa pagitan ng dalawang partido ay makikita sa ibaba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"KEM example using liboqs (local setup required) {#kem-example-using-liboqs-"
"local-setup-required}"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa ng KEM gamit ang liboqs (kailangan ng lokal na setup) {#kem-"
"example-using-liboqs-local-setup-required}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"This example requires some additional local installation, and currently cannot be run on this site. You can review the output below, or alternatively copy the cells to a suitable local environment if you wish to run these examples**\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Ang halimbawang ito ay nangangailangan ng karagdagang lokal na pag-install, at kasalukuyang hindi maaaring patakbuhin sa site na ito. Maaari mong suriin ang output sa ibaba, o kaya ay kopyahin ang mga cell sa isang angkop na lokal na kapaligiran kung nais mong patakbuhin ang mga halimbawang ito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we make use of the algorithms provided by the `liboqs` open source "
"project which provides a libraries for prototyping and experimenting with "
"quantum-safe cryptography. Refer to the links below to setup and test, and "
"then run these examples in your local Python environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito ginagamit natin ang mga algorithm na ibinibigay ng `liboqs` open source"
" project na nagbibigay ng mga library para sa prototyping at eksperimento sa"
" quantum-safe cryptography. Tingnan ang mga link sa ibaba para sa setup at "
"pagsubok, at saka patakbuhin ang mga halimbawang ito sa iyong lokal na "
"Python environment.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Python Library:** This provides the Python language binding for liboqs - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs-Python\n"
msgstr ""
"**Python Library:** Nagbibigay ito ng Python language binding para sa liboqs"
" - https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs-Python\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**liboqs implementation:** This is required by the Python library, and "
"provides the actual algorithm implementations and must be built - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs\n"
msgstr ""
"**liboqs implementation:** Kailangan ito ng Python library, at nagbibigay ng"
" aktwal na mga implementasyon ng algorithm na kailangang i-build - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice wishes to create and securely communicate a shared secret to Bob using"
" a quantum-safe encryption approach. She will use the `Kyber512` KEM "
"algorithm provided by liboqs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nais ni Alice na lumikha at ligtas na maiparating ang isang shared secret "
"kay Bob gamit ang isang quantum-safe na paraan ng encryption. Gagamitin niya"
" ang `Kyber512` KEM algorithm na ibinibigay ng liboqs.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We begin by importing relevant Python modules :\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayo sa pag-import ng mga kaugnay na Python module:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`liboqs` provides a number of KEM implementations and a list of the "
"available algorithms can be easily obtained as follows\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay ang `liboqs` ng maraming implementasyon ng KEM, at madaling "
"makukuha ang listahan ng mga available na algorithm tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that one of the options in the list is `Kyber512` which we will employ in this example. Key exchange using Kyber involves three simple steps namely\n"
"1. Key generation\n"
"2. Encapsulation\n"
"3. Decapsulation\n"
msgstr ""
"Makikita natin na isa sa mga opsyon sa listahan ay ang `Kyber512`, na gagamitin natin sa halimbawang ito. Ang key exchange gamit ang Kyber ay may tatlong simpleng hakbang, katulad ng:\n"
"1. Key generation\n"
"2. Encapsulation\n"
"3. Decapsulation\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the key generation step, the recepient Bob, needs to generate an "
"asymmetric key pair using `Kyber512` and broadcast his public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa hakbang ng key generation, ang tatanggap na si Bob ay kailangang gumawa "
"ng asymmetric key pair gamit ang `Kyber512` at i-broadcast ang kanyang "
"public key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next in the **encapsulation** step, upon receiving Bob's public key, Alice "
"generates both the shared secret and it's corresponding ciphertext using "
"`Kyber512` and Bob's public key. The ciphertext which *encapsulates* the "
"shared secret is then broadcasted to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, sa hakbang ng **encapsulation**, pagkatapos matanggap ang public "
"key ni Bob, si Alice ay gumagawa ng parehong shared secret at ng katumbas na"
" ciphertext gamit ang `Kyber512` at ang public key ni Bob. Ang ciphertext na"
" *nag-eencapsulate* ng shared secret ay ina-broadcast na rin kay Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, in the **decapsulation** step, Bob uses his private key to recover "
"the shared secret from the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, sa hakbang ng **decapsulation**, ginagamit ni Bob ang kanyang "
"private key para mabawi ang shared secret mula sa ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that in contrast to key exchange using RSA, no extraneous padding or "
"key derivation functions are involved here. Kyber's design as a KEM allows "
"for a very minimal user interface while providing the gold standard [**IND-"
"CCA2**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" security for key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na kumpara sa key exchange gamit ang RSA, walang karagdagang padding"
" o key derivation function na kinakailangan dito. Ang disenyo ni Kyber "
"bilang isang KEM ay nagbibigay ng napakasimpleng user interface habang "
"nagbibigay ng gold standard na [**IND-"
"CCA2**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" security para sa key exchange.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IND-CPA and IND-CCA security in lattice-based cryptography {#ind-cpa-and-"
"ind-cca-security-in-lattice-based-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"IND-CPA at IND-CCA security sa lattice-based cryptography {#ind-cpa-and-ind-"
"cca-security-in-lattice-based-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the lesson on Symmetric Key Cryptography, we introduced the notion of "
"**semantic security** or **IND-CPA** security which refers to "
"[**indistinguishability under chosen-plaintext "
"attack**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa aralin tungkol sa Symmetric Key Cryptography, ipinakita natin ang "
"konsepto ng **semantic security** o **IND-CPA** security na tumutukoy sa "
"[**indistinguishability under chosen-plaintext "
"attack**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Traditional cryptosystems whether symmetric (such as AES) or asymmetric "
"(such as RSA) use deterministic functions to implement encryption "
"operations. This means that a given plaintext, combined with a given "
"encryption key will always encrypt to the same ciphertext. Such "
"deterministic cryptosystems are vulnerable to *chosen plaintext attack* "
"whereby an adversary is able to extract information by requesting "
"encryptions of arbitrary plaintexts of their choice from the deterministic "
"encryption function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga tradisyonal na cryptosystem, maging symmetric (tulad ng AES) o "
"asymmetric (tulad ng RSA), ay gumagamit ng mga deterministic na function "
"para ipatupad ang mga operasyon ng encryption. Ibig sabihin, ang isang "
"partikular na plaintext, kasama ang isang partikular na encryption key, ay "
"laging mag-e-encrypt sa parehong ciphertext. Ang mga ganitong deterministic "
"na cryptosystem ay mahina sa *chosen plaintext attack* kung saan ang isang "
"kalaban ay makakakuha ng impormasyon sa pamamagitan ng paghiling ng mga "
"encryption ng mga arbitrary na plaintext na kanilang pinili mula sa "
"deterministic na encryption function.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To achieve IND-CPA security in this context, **additional randomness** is "
"introduced at encryption time either through *initialization vectors* or "
"*padding*. For instance AES is only IND-CPA secure when used in [Cipher "
"Block Chaining (CBC) or Gaolis/Counter Mode (GCM) modes of "
"operation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Block_cipher_mode_of_operation&oldid=1154901199#cite_note-23)"
" that use random initialization vectors. Similarly with RSA, [OAEP "
"padding](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" is need to ensure IND-CPA security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para makamit ang IND-CPA security sa kontekstong ito, **karagdagang "
"randomness** ang isinasama sa oras ng encryption mula sa pamamagitan ng mga "
"*initialization vector* o *padding*. Halimbawa, ang AES ay IND-CPA secure "
"lamang kapag ginagamit sa [Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) o Galois/Counter Mode"
" (GCM) modes of "
"operation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Block_cipher_mode_of_operation&oldid=1154901199#cite_note-23)"
" na gumagamit ng mga random na initialization vector. Katulad nito sa RSA, "
"kailangan ang [OAEP "
"padding](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" para matiyak ang IND-CPA security.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In contrast, lattice-based schemes for encryption are inherently randomized due to the problem definition itself. In particular, in the LWE based encryption scheme outlined above, there are two distinct elements of randomness:\n"
"- **(1)** The error (or noise) $\\varepsilon$ drawn from the distribution $\\chi$\n"
"- **(2)** The random binary vectors $\\mathbf{r} \\in \\{0,1\\}^N$ used for encrypting each bit in the message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kaibahan, ang mga lattice-based scheme para sa encryption ay likas na randomized dahil sa mismong kahulugan ng problema. Sa partikular, sa LWE based encryption scheme na inilabas sa itaas, may dalawang natatanging elemento ng randomness:\n"
"- **(1)** Ang error (o ingay) $\\varepsilon$ na kinukuha mula sa distribusyon $\\chi$\n"
"- **(2)** Ang mga random binary vector $\\mathbf{r} \\in \\{0,1\\}^N$ na ginagamit para i-encrypt ang bawat bit sa mensahe.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The errors $\\varepsilon$ contribute to the security of the public key, "
"ensuring that it's computationally hard to deduce the secret key "
"$\\mathbf{s}$. The random binary vectors $\\mathbf{r}$ on the other hand "
"provide the essential randomness needed for making repeated encryptions of "
"the same plaintext bit non-deterministic. Thus LWE based schemes are "
"considered IND-CPA secure without the need for external mechanisms such as "
"padding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga error na $\\varepsilon$ ay nag-aambag sa seguridad ng public key, "
"tinitiyak na mahirap sa computational na paraan na matuklasan ang secret key"
" $\\mathbf{s}$. Ang mga random binary vector $\\mathbf{r}$ naman ay "
"nagbibigay ng mahalagang randomness na kailangan para gawing hindi-"
"deterministic ang paulit-ulit na pag-encrypt ng parehong plaintext bit. Kaya"
" naman, ang mga LWE based scheme ay itinuturing na IND-CPA secure nang hindi"
" na kailangan ng mga panlabas na mekanismo tulad ng padding.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modern cryptosystems aim to achieve so called [**IND-"
"CCA**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" security which stands for **indistinguishability under chosen-ciphertext "
"attack**. In this setting the adversary has the ability to obtain "
"decryptions of a non-trival set of ciphertexts of their choosing with the "
"aim of extracting information to subsequently break the cryptosystem. A "
"scheme is IND-CCA secure if, even with this capability, the adversary cannot"
" do better than random guessing when trying to distinguish encrypted "
"messages. IND-CCA is a stronger security notion than IND-CPA and subsumes "
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga modernong cryptosystem ay naglalayong makamit ang tinatawag na "
"[**IND-"
"CCA**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" security na nangangahulugang **indistinguishability under chosen-ciphertext"
" attack**. Sa setting na ito, may kakayahan ang kalaban na makakuha ng mga "
"decryption ng isang non-trivial na set ng mga ciphertext na kanilang pinili,"
" na may layuning makuha ang impormasyon para makasira sa cryptosystem. Ang "
"isang scheme ay IND-CCA secure kung, kahit may ganitong kakayahan, ang "
"kalaban ay hindi makakagawa nang mas mabuti kaysa sa random na hulaan kapag "
"sinusubukang makilala ang mga naka-encrypt na mensahe. Ang IND-CCA ay mas "
"malakas na konsepto ng seguridad kaysa sa IND-CPA at sumasaklaw dito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum safe KEMs such as **Kyber** are designed to be IND-CCA secure. This is achieved in two steps:\n"
"1. An IND-CPA secure public key encryption(PKE) scheme is defined. In the case of Kyber such a PKE is based on **Module-LWE**.\n"
"2. A variant of the [Fujisaki-Okamoto transform](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1) (FO) is applied to obtain a CCA-secure KEM. The FO transformation is a generic method to convert encryption schemes that are IND-CPA secure into ones that are IND-CCA secure. For details we refer readers to the [original papers](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga quantum safe KEM tulad ng **Kyber** ay dinisenyo para maging IND-CCA secure. Ito ay nagagawa sa dalawang hakbang:\n"
"1. Isang IND-CPA secure na public key encryption (PKE) scheme ang tinukoy. Sa kaso ng Kyber, ang ganitong PKE ay nakabatay sa **Module-LWE**.\n"
"2. Isang variant ng [Fujisaki-Okamoto transform](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1) (FO) ang inilapat para makakuha ng CCA-secure na KEM. Ang FO transformation ay isang generic na paraan para i-convert ang mga encryption scheme na IND-CPA secure patungong IND-CCA secure. Para sa mga detalye, inirekomenda namin sa mga mambabasa ang [mga orihinal na papel](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more information on the security features of **Kyber** and "
"**Dilithium**, as well as reference implementations in various programming "
"languages, you are encouraged to consult the [CRYSTALS suite "
"documentation](https://pq-crystals.org/).\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa karagdagang impormasyon sa mga tampok ng seguridad ng **Kyber** at "
"**Dilithium**, gayundin ang mga reference implementation sa iba't ibang "
"programming language, hinihikayat kang kumonsulta sa [CRYSTALS suite "
"documentation](https://pq-crystals.org/).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hybrid cryptography {#hybrid-cryptography}"
msgstr "Hybrid cryptography {#hybrid-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hybrid cryptography refers to using quantum-safe public-key algorithms are "
"combined with traditional public key algorithms (like RSA or elliptic "
"curves) such that the solution is at least no less secure than existing "
"traditional cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang hybrid cryptography ay tumutukoy sa paggamit ng mga quantum-safe public-"
"key algorithm na pinagsama sa mga tradisyonal na public key algorithm (tulad"
" ng RSA o elliptic curves) upang ang solusyon ay hindi bababa ang antas ng "
"seguridad kaysa sa kasalukuyang tradisyonal na cryptography.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This can help address 2 issues:\n"
msgstr "Makakatulong ito sa pagtugon sa 2 isyu:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Existing standards may mandate specific algorithms to be used for "
"encryption, or that such algorithms are in some way approved. To add quantum"
" safety, encryption could first be done using the regular algorithm, but "
"then further protected by a quantum-safe algorithm, whilst still meeting "
"required standards.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring itakda ng mga umiiral na pamantayan ang mga partikular na algorithm"
" na gagamitin para sa encryption, o na ang mga ganitong algorithm ay "
"aprubado sa ilang paraan. Para maidagdag ang quantum safety, maaaring gawin "
"muna ang encryption gamit ang regular na algorithm, ngunit saka pa ay higit "
"na protektahan ng isang quantum-safe algorithm, habang naaayon pa rin sa mga"
" kinakailangang pamantayan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum algorithms are new, and further analysis is needed to ensure they "
"are indeed safe and correct. For example one of the initial algorithms "
"shortlisted by NIST was subsequently cracked and proven to be insecure. To "
"mitigate this risk, encryption can be done both using a standard, well-"
"reviewed, secure (apart from quantum!) algorithm, in addition to a post-"
"quantum algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga quantum algorithm ay bago, at kailangan pa ng karagdagang pagsusuri "
"para matiyak na talagang ligtas at tama ang mga ito. Halimbawa, isa sa mga "
"algorithm na inirekomenda ng NIST sa unang pagkakataon ay na-crack at "
"napatunayang hindi secure. Para mabawasan ang panganib na ito, maaaring "
"gawin ang encryption parehong gamit ang isang standard, maayos na nasuri, at"
" secure (maliban sa quantum!) na algorithm, karagdag sa isang post-quantum "
"algorithm.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Buod {#summary}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The migration to quantum-safe cryptography (QSC) of asymmetric key "
"cryptosystems is necessitated by the expected advent of quantum computers "
"that can break traditional asymmetric key algorithms predicated on the "
"classical hardness of NP-intermediate problems. QSC is conjectured to be "
"robust to quantum attacks because its security is based on NP-hard problems,"
" which generally cannot be efficiently solved even with quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang paglipat sa quantum-safe cryptography (QSC) ng mga asymmetric key "
"cryptosystem ay kinakailangan dahil sa inaasahang pagdating ng mga quantum "
"computer na makakabasag sa mga tradisyonal na asymmetric key algorithm na "
"nakabatay sa klasikong kahirapan ng mga NP-intermediate problem. Ang QSC ay "
"itinuturing na matibay laban sa mga quantum attack dahil ang seguridad nito "
"ay nakabatay sa mga NP-hard problem, na karaniwang hindi malulutas nang "
"mahusay kahit gamit ang mga quantum computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this context, hard problems rooted in the theory of mathematical lattices"
" such as the learning with errors (LWE) problem have emerged as leading "
"contenders for QSC standardization. In particular, the CRYSTALS-Kyber and "
"CRYSTALS-Dilithium algorithms, based on modular lattices, are well "
"positioned as near-term alternatives to popular asymmetric key protocols "
"like RSA, Elliptic Curve, Diffie-Hellman, and DSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kontekstong ito, ang mga mahirap na problema na nakaugat sa teorya ng mga"
" mathematical lattice tulad ng learning with errors (LWE) problem ay lumitaw"
" bilang mga nangungunang kandidato para sa QSC standardization. Sa "
"partikular, ang mga algorithm na CRYSTALS-Kyber at CRYSTALS-Dilithium, na "
"nakabatay sa mga modular lattice, ay nasa magandang posisyon bilang mga "
"malapit-na-panahon na alternatibo sa mga popular na asymmetric key protocol "
"tulad ng RSA, Elliptic Curve, Diffie-Hellman, at DSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we navigate the complex landscape of quantum-safe cryptography, embracing"
" these innovative solutions will be pivotal in upholding the integrity and "
"confidentiality of our digital interactions in the quantum era.\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang tinatahak natin ang kumplikadong tanawin ng quantum-safe "
"cryptography, ang pagtanggap sa mga makabagong solusyong ito ay magiging "
"susi sa pagpapanatili ng integridad at kumpidensyalidad ng ating mga digital"
" na pakikipag-ugnayan sa panahon ng quantum.\n"
